Task 1: Set up Molecule for Testing Ansible Playbooks
Subtask 1.1: Update System and Install Prerequisites
First, update your system and install the necessary packages.

# Update package repositories
sudo apt update

# Install Python3 and pip if not already installed
sudo apt install -y python3 python3-pip python3-venv git

# Install Docker for container-based testing
sudo apt install -y docker.io

# Add current user to docker group
sudo usermod -aG docker $USER

# Apply group changes (logout and login, or use newgrp)
newgrp docker

# Verify Docker installation
docker --version
Subtask 1.2: Create Python Virtual Environment
Create an isolated Python environment for Molecule and its dependencies.

# Create a directory for the lab
mkdir -p ~/ansible-molecule-lab
cd ~/ansible-molecule-lab

# Create Python virtual environment
python3 -m venv molecule-env

# Activate the virtual environment
source molecule-env/bin/activate

# Upgrade pip to latest version
pip install --upgrade pip
Subtask 1.3: Install Molecule and Dependencies
Install Molecule along with required plugins and dependencies.

# Install Molecule with Docker driver
pip install molecule[docker]

# Install additional dependencies
pip install ansible-core
pip install molecule-plugins[docker]
pip install docker

# Verify installations
molecule --version
ansible --version
