Task 2: Write a Test Case to Verify Playbook Functionality
Subtask 2.1: Create a Simple Web Server Role
Develop a basic Ansible role that installs and configures a web server.

# Edit the main tasks file
nano tasks/main.yml
Add the following content to tasks/main.yml:

---
# tasks file for webserver
- name: Update apt cache
  apt:
    update_cache: yes
  become: yes

- name: Install Apache web server
  apt:
    name: apache2
    state: present
  become: yes

- name: Start and enable Apache service
  systemd:
    name: apache2
    state: started
    enabled: yes
  become: yes

- name: Create a custom index.html
  copy:
    content: |
      <html>
      <head><title>Test Web Server</title></head>
      <body>
        <h1>Hello from Ansible Molecule Test!</h1>
        <p>This web server was configured by Ansible.</p>
      </body>
      </html>
    dest: /var/www/html/index.html
    owner: www-data
    group: www-data
    mode: '0644'
  become: yes

- name: Ensure Apache is listening on port 80
  lineinfile:
    path: /etc/apache2/ports.conf
    regexp: '^Listen 80'
    line: 'Listen 80'
  become: yes
  notify: restart apache2
Subtask 2.2: Create Handlers
Create handlers for service management.

# Edit the handlers file
nano handlers/main.yml
Add the following content to handlers/main.yml:

---
# handlers file for webserver
- name: restart apache2
  systemd:
    name: apache2
    state: restarted
  become: yes

- name: reload apache2
  systemd:
    name: apache2
    state: reloaded
  become: yes
Subtask 2.3: Configure Molecule Test Instance
Modify the Molecule configuration to use Ubuntu for testing.

# Edit the Molecule configuration
nano molecule/default/molecule.yml
Replace the content with:

---
dependency:
  name: galaxy
driver:
  name: docker
platforms:
  - name: instance
    image: ubuntu:20.04
    pre_build_image: true
    privileged: true
    volumes:
      - /sys/fs/cgroup:/sys/fs/cgroup:ro
    command: /lib/systemd/systemd
    tmpfs:
      - /run
      - /tmp
    capabilities:
      - SYS_ADMIN
provisioner:
  name: ansible
  config_options:
    defaults:
      interpreter_python: auto_silent
      callback_whitelist: profile_tasks, timer, yaml
    ssh_connection:
      pipelining: false
verifier:
  name: ansible
Subtask 2.4: Update the Converge Playbook
Modify the converge playbook to apply the webserver role.

# Edit the converge playbook
nano molecule/default/converge.yml
Replace the content with:

---
- name: Converge
  hosts: all
  become: true
  gather_facts: true
  roles:
    - role: webserver
Subtask 2.5: Create Comprehensive Test Cases
Write detailed test cases to verify the web server functionality.

# Edit the verify playbook
nano molecule/default/verify.yml
Replace the content with:

---
- name: Verify
  hosts: all
  gather_facts: false
  tasks:
    - name: Check if Apache2 package is installed
      package_facts:
        manager: apt
      become: true

    - name: Verify Apache2 is installed
      assert:
        that:
          - "'apache2' in ansible_facts.packages"
        fail_msg: "Apache2 package is not installed"
        success_msg: "Apache2 package is successfully installed"

    - name: Check Apache2 service status
      systemd:
        name: apache2
      register: apache_status
      become: true

    - name: Verify Apache2 service is running
      assert:
        that:
          - apache_status.status.ActiveState == "active"
        fail_msg: "Apache2 service is not running"
        success_msg: "Apache2 service is running successfully"

    - name: Verify Apache2 service is enabled
      assert:
        that:
          - apache_status.status.UnitFileState == "enabled"
        fail_msg: "Apache2 service is not enabled"
        success_msg: "Apache2 service is enabled"

    - name: Check if Apache is listening on port 80
      wait_for:
        port: 80
        host: localhost
        timeout: 10
      become: true

    - name: Verify custom index.html exists
      stat:
        path: /var/www/html/index.html
      register: index_file
      become: true

    - name: Assert index.html file exists
      assert:
        that:
          - index_file.stat.exists
        fail_msg: "Custom index.html file does not exist"
        success_msg: "Custom index.html file exists"

    - name: Check index.html content
      slurp:
        src: /var/www/html/index.html
      register: index_content
      become: true

    - name: Verify index.html contains expected content
      assert:
        that:
          - "'Hello from Ansible Molecule Test!' in (index_content.content | b64decode)"
        fail_msg: "Index.html does not contain expected content"
        success_msg: "Index.html contains the expected content"

    - name: Test HTTP response
      uri:
        url: http://localhost
        method: GET
        return_content: yes
      register: http_response
      become: true

    - name: Verify HTTP response is successful
      assert:
        that:
          - http_response.status == 200
          - "'Hello from Ansible Molecule Test!' in http_response.content"
        fail_msg: "HTTP response test failed"
        success_msg: "HTTP response test passed successfully"
